node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
.env.e2e

# A-08 precheck output is deliberately NOT committed, unlike its sibling
# a11y-report/axe-results.json. The axe file is a frozen acceptance artifact;
# this one is whatever a developer's last local run produced. Committed, it
# would sit beside the audit worksheet looking like recorded evidence for an
# audit that has not happened. CI uploads it as a build artifact instead.
a11y-report/precheck-results.json

# Same reasoning, and the same hazard observed while preparing A-08: a local
# `npm run a11y` writes these two next to the tracked axe evidence, and they are
# easy to commit by accident. They are re-baselining INPUT — you copy their
# contents into a11y-baseline.json — never a record in their own right.
a11y-report/axe-baseline.measured.json
a11y-report/axe-baseline.tightened.json

# The Lighthouse ratchet's re-baselining INPUT, ignored for exactly the reason
# above: you copy their contents into lighthouse-baseline.json's `floors`. A
# committed `measured` file would sit beside the tracked lighthouse-results.json
# looking like a second, rival floor. CI uploads both as build artifacts.
lighthouse-report/lighthouse-baseline.measured.json
lighthouse-report/lighthouse-baseline.tightened.json
